The game's own Lua name, from the baked-in registration at 0x8F68D1 (RTTI `float CEU3AI::EvaluateCancelTrades(float, GoodsCategory)`). Read whole 2026-10-13, 0x89B810 to the `ret 8` at 0x89BC7B. **The engine's own code for an AI giving up exports of one good, called only from Lua**:

    if (amount <= 0) return amount
    for each country o of the game state's country vector, o != us,
      for each route r on us->diplomacy[o]->trade_routes:
        v = (us == r.from ? r.trade_from (+0x44) : r.trade_to (+0x34))[category] / 1000.0   ; what we hand over
        if v > 0:
          if v > amount: keep r as a candidate
          else:          amount -= v; PostTradeRouteCancel(r)
    if amount > 0 and there are candidates:
        PostTradeRouteCancel(the candidate with the smallest v, the first of equals); amount = 0
    return amount

So every export of the good no larger than what is still to be freed is cancelled, in country order and list order, and then the smallest larger one. Each cancellation is a posted command, so it takes effect when the command executes.
